nodecode-costguard is a rewrite of Whydiriki700's Whydiriki700/costguard:

  https://github.com/Whydiriki700/costguard
  commit 967e2b7ac9fed33698d430906bd6feba0339a6fe
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Riki Wahyudi (LICENSE)

What was rewritten: the plugin's four pieces are one cell. Its metering of
each API call from the provider's usage block became a read of the
`turn.usage` facts Nodecode already records per provider round — exact
counts, and the cost the catalog's price made of them at the time of the
round; its per-session and per-day totals are folded from those facts; its
nudge as a budget nears is one line recorded into the turn at the round
point, once per session and level; and its brake is a refusal at the tool
point, with the same exemption for its own status tool. The `/cost` command,
the status tool and the manual carry the report.

What was left out, and why: the per-model price overrides in the plugin's
settings are dropped, because Nodecode prices each round with its own catalog
when the round is recorded and that price is what the store keeps; the
chars-per-token estimate for endpoints that report no usage is dropped too,
because a round with no counts is metered as nothing rather than guessed at,
and the plugin's own unit-test suite is replaced by this cell's tests.
